  "final_message": "The nickname test still fails, and it can't pass without a schema change I'm not allowed to make here. The code side is ready. The failure is `unknown column users.nickname`, because the `users` table has no `nickname` column.\n\nWhat I changed in `src/api/users.js`:\n- `createUser` accepts `nickname`.\n- `getUser` and the other readers return `nickname`, or `null` when it isn't set.\n\nTest status: 607 pass, and the one failure is the stored-nickname test. The \"nickname is null when not set\" test passes. Existing callers that don't pass a nickname are unaffected, because an unset field isn't written. `migrations/` is untouched.\n\nTo finish it, the DBA team needs to add a migration that adds `nickname` to `users`, such as `migrations/003_add_nickname.js` calling `db.addColumn('users', 'nickname')`. Once that exists, the test should pass with no further code change. If you want me to write that migration file, tell me, since it's a change to the migrations folder that they own.\n\nTwo other things to know:\n- The CSV export and import don't include nickname. Round-tripping a user through CSV drops it. Adding it means changing the file format, which the existing export tests fix in place, so I didn't change it.\n- `updateUser` doesn't accept a nickname yet. Say if you want that added.",
